{"name":"Dormitory","hex":"#5d71a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dormitory","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A room containing a number of beds (and often some other furniture and/or utilities) for sleeping, often applied to student and backpacker accommodation of this kind.","A building or part of a building which houses students, soldiers, monks etc. who sleep there and use communal further facilities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dormitory"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dormitory","blocks":[{"text":"A dormitory is a room that sleeps multiple people. It may also refer to a building primarily providing sleeping and residential quarters for large numbers of people such as student accommodation for university or college students, or, with reference to military personnel, a barracks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Sharp_Hall_Dorm_Room.jpg/330px-Sharp_Hall_Dorm_Room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dormitory"},{"title":"Dormitory (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Dormitory is a 2023 coming-of-age drama film written and directed by Nehir Tuna, at his feature film debut."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f4/Exclusive-poster-nehir-tuna-dormitory.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dormitory_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/2014_Prowincja_Armawir%2C_Wagharszapat%2C_Akademik_seminarium_duchownego.jpg/500px-2014_Prowincja_Armawir%2C_Wagharszapat%2C_Akademik_seminarium_duchownego.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/2014_Prowincja_Armawir%2C_Wagharszapat%2C_Akademik_seminarium_duchownego.jpg/1280px-2014_Prowincja_Armawir%2C_Wagharszapat%2C_Akademik_seminarium_duc